    "result_text": "All 268 tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the owner initials feature by adding an `initials` field to the owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (which drives generation of `OwnerDto`), documented as the first letter of the first and last name, upper-cased and dot-separated with a trailing dot.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that computes `initials` from the owner's first and last name:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\" + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n\nThis mirrors the existing `displayName` mapping approach, so the `initials` field is populated on every `OwnerDto` returned \u2014 including the create/add owner response (e.g. John Smith \u2192 `J.S.`). The full test suite (268 tests) passes green.",
